-- Continue migrating the remaining 2 publications

-- 3. Web2 vs Web3 Marketing
UPDATE public.page_translations pt
SET 
  title = 'Web2 vs Web3 Marketing: Why Ownership Beats Attention',
  meta_description = 'A practical breakdown of the shift from renting attention to building ownership - with examples, principles, and a simple framework.',
  content = '<article class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none"><p class="text-lg">When I transitioned from professional swimming to marketing, I learned that discipline isn''t about doing more - it''s about doing what matters. In the pool, every stroke counts. In Web2 marketing, every click counted. But in Web3, every relationship counts more than any metric.</p><p class="text-lg">Marketing isn''t dying - it''s evolving from capturing attention to building ownership. And that changes everything.</p><h2 id="architecture" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The Fundamental Architecture: Two Different Worlds</h2><p>Marketing is evolving from capturing attention to building ownership. Web2 optimized for reach on centralized platforms; Web3 optimizes for direct, verifiable relationships with stakeholders.</p><div class="my-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Web2: Platform Economy</h3><ul class="space-y-2"><li>📊 Centralized data - platforms own everything</li><li>💰 Algorithmic distribution - pay to play</li><li>🔒 Intermediary-dependent - no direct access</li><li>📉 Data extraction model - users are the product</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Web3: Ownership Economy</h3><ul class="space-y-2"><li>🔓 Decentralized data - users own wallets and identity</li><li>🤝 Direct relationships - no middlemen</li><li>✅ Transparent verification - on-chain proof</li><li>📈 Value co-creation - users become stakeholders</li></ul></div></div><p>For two decades, marketing meant renting attention on someone else''s platform. Facebook owned your audience. Google controlled your visibility. You paid to reach people you couldn''t truly own.</p><p>Web3 flips this. Instead of renting attention, you build relationships with stakeholders. Instead of paying platforms, you reward communities for contribution.</p><div class="my-8 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-primary bg-muted/50 p-6"><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">💡 Key Insight</h3><p>82% of Web3 marketers report positive ROI from community ownership models, with 2–4x efficiency gains versus traditional campaigns.</p></div><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10">Real Example: Starbucks Odyssey</h2><div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 my-6"><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-3">← Traditional rewards (Web2)</h4><ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm"><li>• Earn stars through purchases</li><li>• Locked in ecosystem</li><li>• No transferability</li><li>• Company controls terms</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-3">→ Starbucks Odyssey (Web3)</h4><ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm"><li>• Earn NFT "journey stamps"</li><li>• True ownership</li><li>• Tradeable on markets</li><li>• Community-driven value</li></ul></div></div><p>The result? Loyalty becomes tangible. Engagement becomes an asset. Customers become advocates because they own a piece of the story.</p><p>This isn''t about replacing loyalty programs with tokens. It''s asking: What if customers could own their relationship with your brand?</p><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10">The Philosophy Shift: Attention → Ownership</h2><table class="w-full my-6 border"><thead class="bg-muted text-left"><tr><th class="p-3">Mindset</th><th class="p-3">Web2</th><th class="p-3">Web3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Goal</td><td class="p-3">Extract value</td><td class="p-3">Co-create value</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">User is…</td><td class="p-3">Customer</td><td class="p-3">Stakeholder</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Success =</td><td class="p-3">Conversion</td><td class="p-3">Ownership</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Timeline</td><td class="p-3">Quarterly</td><td class="p-3">Long-term</td></tr></tbody></table><blockquote class="my-6 border-l-4 border-primary pl-4 italic"><p>Web2 assumption: Attention is scarce, capture and monetize it.</p><p>Web3 assumption: Ownership is powerful, distribute and nurture it.</p></blockquote><p>When you give people real ownership - not points, but tradeable value - they don''t just engage differently. They think differently. They become evangelists, strategists, and builders. Because now, it''s their project too.</p><h2 id="principles" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">5 Core Principles Marketers Must Learn</h2><div class="space-y-6 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">1. Transparency Is Non-Negotiable</h3><p>In Web2, we crafted narratives. In Web3, we prove them. Every claim can be verified on-chain. If you say "70% of tokens go to community," anyone can check the blockchain.</p><p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary">Action: Practice radical transparency. Share real numbers. Let the community verify your claims.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">2. Community Is Your Distribution</h3><p>The best Web3 projects don''t have traditional marketing departments. They have communities that organically promote because they have economic alignment (tokens) and emotional alignment (shared mission).</p><div class="my-4 rounded-lg bg-muted/50 p-4 text-center border border-primary/20"><p class="text-sm font-semibold">📊 Web3 projects with active communities see 4x higher user retention vs. traditional models</p></div><p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary">Action: Ask "How can our community market this?" before "How can we market this?"</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">3. Incentive Design &gt; Campaign Design</h3><p>Instead of spending $100K on ads, some Web3 projects distribute $100K in tokens to early contributors who create content, report bugs, or participate in governance.</p><p>Traditional ads rent attention temporarily. Token incentives create long-term stakeholders.</p><p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary">Action: Learn basic tokenomics. Reward contribution, not just consumption.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">4. Data Privacy Is a Feature</h3><p>You might only know someone''s wallet address, but you know exactly what they''ve done on-chain: tokens held, protocols used, NFTs collected, DAOs joined.</p><p>Behavioral targeting based on on-chain activity is more predictive than demographic targeting.</p><p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary">Action: Shift from demographic (who they are) to behavioral (what they do on-chain) targeting.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">5. Long-Term Thinking Wins</h3><p>Web2 optimizes for quarters. Web3 optimizes for decades.</p><p>You''re not building a customer base - you''re building an ecosystem that can outlive your company.</p><p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary">Action: Track community health, holder retention, and network effects - not just acquisition.</p></div></div><h2 id="hybrid" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The Hybrid Future: Best of Both Worlds</h2><p>The smartest brands don''t choose - they blend.</p><div class="my-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-3">Use Web2 for:</h4><ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm"><li>✓ Education &amp; awareness</li><li>✓ Mainstream reach</li><li>✓ Paid acquisition</li><li>✓ Content at scale</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-3">Use Web3 for:</h4><ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm"><li>✓ Deep engagement</li><li>✓ Long-term retention</li><li>✓ Transparent incentives</li><li>✓ Network effects</li></ul></div></div><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8">Nike''s Approach</h3><p>Nike didn''t abandon Instagram ads. They added .SWOOSH (their Web3 platform) for superfans. Web2 brings them in. Web3 keeps them invested.</p><div class="my-8 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-primary bg-muted/50 p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold">Over 1M AI agents expected on blockchain networks by end of 2025 - marketing to non-humans is coming faster than you think.</p></div><p><strong>The AI Layer:</strong> AI bridges Web2 and Web3, enabling on-chain analytics, churn prediction, fraud detection, and personalization while respecting privacy.</p><h2 id="leaders" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">What This Means For You</h2><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">For Marketing Leaders</h3><table class="w-full my-6 border"><thead class="bg-muted text-left"><tr><th class="p-3">0-6 Months</th><th class="p-3">6-12 Months</th><th class="p-3">12-24 Months</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t align-top"><td class="p-3"><ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5"><li>Get a wallet</li><li>Join a DAO</li><li>Hire/train</li></ul></td><td class="p-3"><ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5"><li>Build on-chain attribution</li><li>Run 1 experiment</li><li>Prep for AI agents</li></ul></td><td class="p-3"><ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5"><li>Design ownership model</li><li>Launch token-gated pilot</li><li>Implement hybrid metrics</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8">For Individual Marketers</h3><p>Your existing skills aren''t obsolete - they''re foundational. Knowing how to craft messages, analyze funnels, and build relationships? That''s still 80% of the job.</p><h4 class="font-semibold mt-6">Add to your skillset:</h4><ul class="space-y-2 my-4"><li>□ Basic blockchain literacy (wallets, smart contracts, DAOs)</li><li>□ On-chain analytics (Dune, Nansen, Formo)</li><li>□ Community management 2.0 (Discord, governance)</li><li>□ AI fundamentals (segmentation, prediction, fraud detection)</li></ul><div class="my-8 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 p-6 text-center"><p class="italic">When I made this transition, I felt like a beginner again. That discomfort was the point. The marketers who thrive aren''t the ones who resist change - they''re the ones who stay curious.</p></div><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2><table class="w-full my-6 border"><tbody><tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Web1 (1990s)</td><td class="p-3">Information Broadcasting</td></tr><tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Web2 (2000s-2020s)</td><td class="p-3">Engagement Optimization</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Web3 (2020s+)</td><td class="p-3">Ownership Alignment</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The shift from Web2 to Web3 isn''t just about technology. It''s about rediscovering what marketing should have been all along: creating genuine value for real people.</p><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8">What Stays the Same:</h3><ul class="my-4"><li>Know your audience deeply</li><li>Communicate with clarity</li><li>Build trust through consistency</li><li>Create more value than you capture</li></ul><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6">What Must Change:</h3><p>You can''t optimize for ownership the way you optimized for attention. You can''t measure Web3 value with Web2 metrics.</p><blockquote class="my-6 border-l-4 border-primary pl-4 text-lg font-medium italic"><p>"The future belongs to marketers who respect what worked AND embrace what''s emerging."</p><footer class="mt-2 text-sm font-normal not-italic">- Gabriel Mangabeira</footer></blockquote><h2 id="first-steps" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">Start Here: Your First Steps</h2><div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 my-6"><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">1. Experience It</h4><ul class="mb-4 space-y-1 text-sm"><li>• Download MetaMask</li><li>• Join a DAO</li><li>• Mint a free NFT</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">2. Follow Signal</h4><ul class="mb-4 space-y-1 text-sm"><li>• The Defiant</li><li>• Bankless</li><li>• a16z crypto</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">3. Experiment</h4><ul class="mb-4 space-y-1 text-sm"><li>• Token-gate content</li><li>• Create comm wallet</li><li>• Launch small NFT</li></ul></div></div><h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="space-y-4 my-6"><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">1. What is the main difference between Web2 and Web3 marketing?</h4><p class="text-sm">Web2 marketing focuses on capturing attention through centralized platforms where companies own user data. Web3 marketing emphasizes community ownership, where users control their data and become stakeholders through tokens.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">2. How can traditional marketers transition to Web3?</h4><p class="text-sm">Start by experiencing Web3 firsthand: create a wallet, join a DAO, and mint an NFT. Then build on-chain attribution, learn tokenomics basics, and run small experiments with token-gated content.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-5"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">3. Do I need to abandon Web2 marketing for Web3?</h4><p class="text-sm">No. The most effective approach is hybrid: use Web2 for awareness and reach, while implementing Web3 principles for retention and community building. Brands like Nike and Starbucks successfully blend both.</p></div></div><div class="my-12 rounded-lg border-2 border-primary bg-primary/5 p-8 text-center"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Ready to Dive Deeper?</h3><p class="mb-6 text-lg">Let''s discuss how these principles can apply to your business.</p><a href="https://calendly.com/gabriel-mangabeira/15min" target="_blank" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-foreground font-medium hover:bg-primary/90">Work With Me</a></div></article>'
FROM pages p
WHERE pt.page_id = p.id
AND p.slug = 'web2-vs-web3-marketing'
AND pt.language = 'en';

-- 4. Web3 SEO Guide (largest content piece - simplified version with key sections)
UPDATE public.page_translations pt
SET 
  title = 'Web3 SEO in 2025 and Beyond: Your Strategic Guide to Decentralized Discovery',
  meta_description = 'Comprehensive guide to Web3 SEO covering decentralized search engines, on-chain ranking factors, GEO optimization, and strategic frameworks for blockchain projects.',
  content = '<article class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none"><div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-300/40 bg-amber-100/10 p-5 mb-8"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-2xl">⚠️</span><div><div class="font-semibold">Critical shift happening now</div><p class="text-sm">A 25% drop in traditional search traffic is predicted by 2026. AI chat answers are rewriting discoverability.</p></div></div></div><h2 id="paradigm" class="text-2xl font-bold">The Paradigm Shift: Web2 vs Web3 Search</h2><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Web2 Search</h3><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">Centralized discovery</p><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>• Google as gatekeeper</li><li>• Opaque algorithms</li><li>• Data = their asset</li><li>• Trust = inferred</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Web3 Search</h3><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">Decentralized discovery</p><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>• Multiple engines</li><li>• Transparent ranking</li><li>• Data = your asset</li><li>• Trust = verifiable</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Your Strategy</h3><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">Hybrid approach</p><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>• On-chain + off-chain</li><li>• Community-driven</li><li>• AI-optimized</li><li>• Future-proof</li></ul></div></div><h2 id="ecosystem" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The New Search Ecosystem</h2><div class="space-y-6 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Decentralized Search Engines</h3><ul class="space-y-3"><li><strong>Presearch:</strong> Community-powered. Token incentives (PRE).</li><li><strong>Brave Search:</strong> Privacy-first. Independent index.</li><li><strong>YaCy (P2P):</strong> Peer-to-peer, community index.</li></ul><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Reality check: Google still controls the vast majority of search traffic today. Your strategy must be bilingual: optimize for Google now and build for Web3 dominance long-term.</p></div></div><h2 id="onchain" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The New Ranking Factors: On-Chain Authority</h2><table class="w-full my-8 border"><thead class="bg-muted"><tr><th class="p-3 text-left">Factor</th><th class="p-3 text-left">Web2 (Google)</th><th class="p-3 text-left">Web3 (Decentralized)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Primary Signal</td><td class="p-3">Backlinks, domain authority</td><td class="p-3">On-chain validation, token staking</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Trust Proof</td><td class="p-3">Media mentions, E-E-A-T</td><td class="p-3">Audits, blockchain records</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Content Auth</td><td class="p-3">Author bio, credentials</td><td class="p-3">Signed on-chain publishing</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Community</td><td class="p-3">Social shares (likes)</td><td class="p-3">DAO votes, governance participation</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Identity</td><td class="p-3">Email, social logins</td><td class="p-3">Wallet + verifiable credentials</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="space-y-4 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">On-Chain Validation</h4><p class="text-sm">Publishing content via Mirror, Arweave, or IPFS provides immutable proof of authorship. A whitepaper on-chain has verifiable timestamps; a copy on Medium is not.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Token-Based Reputation</h4><p class="text-sm">Staking and governance participation are economic trust signals. Design token utility with reputation in mind to build durable authority.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Wallet History as Credit Score</h4><p class="text-sm">Wallets with long history, reputable interactions, and blue-chip holdings carry more weight than new wallets. Engage authoritative wallets to amplify ranking signals.</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Smart Contract Metadata</h4><p class="text-sm">Clear names, verified source code, and descriptive metadata function like on-page SEO for contracts—improving discovery in explorers and aggregators.</p></div></div><h2 id="framework" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">Your Strategic Framework: The Hybrid Approach</h2><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">On-Chain SEO</h3><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">Verifiable authority</p><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>✓ Smart contract optimization</li><li>✓ Blockchain domain (.eth)</li><li>✓ On-chain content publishing</li><li>✓ Token-gated experiences</li><li>✓ DAO governance content</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Off-Chain SEO</h3><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">Immediate visibility</p><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>✓ Traditional keyword research</li><li>✓ Educational content</li><li>✓ Crypto media backlinks</li><li>✓ Community building</li><li>✓ Technical site optimization</li></ul></div></div><h2 id="geo" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The AI Revolution: Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)</h2><div class="rounded-lg border border-red-300/40 bg-red-100/10 p-5 mb-8"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-2xl">⚠️</span><div><div class="font-semibold">64% drop in clicks when AI Overviews appear</div><p class="text-sm">Traditional SEO aims for #1. GEO aims to be cited inside the AI answer.</p></div></div></div><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Structured Data</h4><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Schema.org, FAQs, tables, definitions</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Brand Authority</h4><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Verified sources, media mentions</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border p-6"><h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">AI Crawl Access</h4><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Allow GPTBot, Perplexity, Claude-Web</p></div></div><h2 id="analytics" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The Analytics Stack: Measuring What Matters</h2><table class="w-full my-8 border"><thead class="bg-muted"><tr><th class="p-3 text-left">Category</th><th class="p-3 text-left">Tools</th><th class="p-3 text-left">What It Tracks</th><th class="p-3 text-left">Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">On-Chain Intel</td><td class="p-3">Dune, Nansen, The Graph</td><td class="p-3">Competitor metrics, wallet behavior, trends</td><td class="p-3">$50–500/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Attribution</td><td class="p-3">Formo, Spindl, Cookie3</td><td class="p-3">Off-chain → on-chain journey</td><td class="p-3">$300–3K/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Traditional SEO</td><td class="p-3">Ahrefs, Semrush, GSC</td><td class="p-3">Keywords, backlinks, rankings</td><td class="p-3">$100–500/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Platform Tracking</td><td class="p-3">DappRadar, Presearch Analytics</td><td class="p-3">dApp store ranking, DSE visibility</td><td class="p-3">Free–$200/mo</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="my-6 rounded-lg border bg-muted/40 p-4"><p class="font-semibold mb-2">The attribution breakthrough</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Connect Google Search → Website → Wallet connect → On-chain swap. Finally, marketing spend maps to revenue.</p></div><h2 id="plan" class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">Your Action Plan</h2><div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 my-8"><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Pre-Launch</h3><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>Set up documentation (quickstart, concepts, tutorials)</li><li>Claim ENS and configure records</li><li>Enable analytics and basic attribution</li><li>Seed your community channels</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Post-Launch</h3><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>Ship pillar pages and comparison pages</li><li>Integrate GEO (FAQ, structured data, robots.txt)</li><li>Publish audits and verifiable on-chain content</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Scaling</h3><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>Expand content clusters; build digital PR</li><li>Track wallet connects → on-chain actions</li><li>Optimize smart contract metadata</li></ul></div><div class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-l-primary p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Enterprise</h3><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm"><li>Full hybrid strategy across org</li><li>Advanced attribution and LTV modeling</li><li>Governance content and rigorous audits</li></ul></div></div><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12">The Bottom Line: Authority is Verifiable</h2><blockquote class="my-8 rounded-lg border bg-muted/40 p-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>"Web3 SEO is not about gaming algorithms. It''s about building verifiable authority that machines can trust and communities can validate."</p></blockquote><div class="my-12 rounded-lg border-2 border-primary bg-primary/5 p-8 text-center"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Ready to Master Web3 SEO?</h3><p class="mb-6 text-lg">Let''s discuss how to implement a hybrid SEO strategy for your Web3 project.</p><a href="https://calendly.com/gabriel-mangabeira/15min" target="_blank" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-primary text-primary-foreground font-medium hover:bg-primary/90">Work With Me</a></div></article>'
FROM pages p
WHERE pt.page_id = p.id
AND p.slug = 'definitive-guide-web3-seo'
AND pt.language = 'en';